The game accepts _either_ the symbol for the class of monsters, _or_
any substring of the class description. Let's take 's' as an example;
/-examining one gives

s       an arachnid or centipede (cave spider)--More--

and, indeed, blessed-genociding 'arachnid' or 'centipede' will
genocide all 's'. (Or 'chni', or 'tipe'; 'ent' will, however, genocide
all 'r', since 'rodent' happens to match that substring first.)

Naming a monster in that class isn't sufficient, unless it happens to
be part of this description, as it is for liches; trying to
blessed-genocide 'demilich' won't get you anywhere.

> I have never tried it myself and I don't know whether it matters if
> you use singular "lich" or plural "liches" and so on.

The string you enter is singularised first, so 'liches' would be fine.
(It handles things like 'fungi' and 'vortices' as well.)

